---
// DRAFT privacy notice — the owner must review and complete every [placeholder]
// before the forms go live. It describes what this site actually does: two
// forms via Web3Forms, WhatsApp links, Stripe Payment Links, Netlify hosting,
// Google Fonts. Update it if any of those change.
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import Prose from "../components/Prose.astro";
import { EMAIL } from "../site";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy notice · LightCakes" description="How LightCakes uses the personal details you share with us.">
	<PageHeader
		title="Privacy notice"
		intro="What we collect when you get in touch or order, why, and what you can ask us to do with it."
	/>

	<Prose>
		<p><em>Last updated: [date]</em></p>

		<h2>Who we are</h2>
		<p>
			LightCakes is run by Abimbola Ademoluti, based in Leeds, UK. We're responsible for the personal details
			you share with us. You can contact us about anything on this page at {EMAIL}.
		</p>

		<h2>What we collect</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>When you send an enquiry or ask for a quote:</strong> your name, email address and, if you give them, your
				phone number, company name, delivery postcode, budget and the details of your order.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Allergies and dietary requirements,</strong> if you tell us about them. This can count as health information,
				so we only use it to make your order safely.
			</li>
			<li><strong>When you message us on WhatsApp:</strong> your phone number and your messages.</li>
			<li>
				<strong>When you order from our shop:</strong> payment is handled by Stripe. We receive your name, email, delivery
				address, phone number and anything you add at checkout (such as your delivery date) — never your card details.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Why we use it</h2>
		<p>
			Only to reply to you, quote for, make and deliver your order, and send invoices. We use it because you've asked us
			to and it's needed to take your order. We don't send marketing emails, and we never sell or share your details for
			anyone else's marketing.
		</p>

		<h2>Who else handles it</h2>
		<p>We use a few trusted services to run the website and take orders:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Web3Forms</strong> delivers the website's forms to our email inbox.</li>
			<li><strong>Stripe</strong> takes payments and sends invoices.</li>
			<li><strong>WhatsApp</strong> (Meta), if you choose to message us there.</li>
			<li><strong>Netlify</strong> hosts the website.</li>
			<li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> supplies the website's fonts, so Google sees your IP address when a page loads.</li>
			<li>[Email provider, e.g. Google Workspace or Microsoft 365], where our emails are stored.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>The website doesn't use cookies or tracking.</p>

		<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
		<p>
			[Enquiries that don't become orders: deleted after X months. Orders and invoices: kept for as long as HMRC
			requires — confirm the period with your accountant.]
		</p>

		<h2>Your rights</h2>
		<p>
			You can ask us for a copy of the details we hold about you, to correct them, or to delete them. Email
			{EMAIL} and we'll reply within one month.
		</p>
		<p>
			If you're unhappy with how we've handled your details, please tell us first. You can also complain to the
			Information Commissioner's Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ico.org.uk</a>.
		</p>
	</Prose>
</BaseLayout>
